Teach the native DFlash context-KV fusion to consume the compressed-tensors
WNA16 loader representation. The draft checkpoint uses symmetric W4A16 group
quantization, so QKVParallelLinear owns weight_packed and weight_scale rather
than a dense weight parameter while load_weights runs.

The normal compressed-tensors loader and the later Marlin repack stay
unchanged. Only the KV rows the one-time fused context projection buffer needs
are materialized; asymmetric and activation-ordered layouts fail closed.

